ANONYMIZER — LB IT CLOUD — COPYRIGHT AND TERMS

Copyright (c) 2026 LB IT Cloud SAS, France. All rights reserved.

This repository publishes the source of the Anonymizer, a free tool of the LB IT
Cloud website (https://www.lbitcloud.com/anonymizer), so that anyone can read the
code that runs in their browser and check that the offline file is built from
it. It is not open-source software: it is published to be read and verified.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

1. Read, review and audit this source; discuss it, report on it and quote short
   extracts of it with attribution.

2. Rebuild the offline file from this source and run its tests, in order to
   verify it.

3. Use the Anonymizer — on the website, or the offline file
   (anonymizer-offline.html) downloaded from the website or from this
   repository — unmodified, to anonymize your own texts and documents, including
   in your work and for your clients; keep copies of the offline file for that
   use, and make it available, unmodified, to the members of your organisation
   for the same use, for instance on its intranet.


WHAT IS NOT GRANTED

Any other use. In particular, without the written agreement of LB IT Cloud SAS:
copying, modifying, adapting, merging, publishing, distributing, sublicensing or
selling this source or the offline file, in whole or in part, or including them
in another product, service or website.


NO WARRANTY

The Anonymizer reduces the risk of sharing confidential data; it does not
guarantee that a text or a document is anonymous, and it detects only what its
dictionary and its patterns recognise. Read every result before you share it.
The source and the offline file are provided "as is", without warranty of any
kind, express or implied. To the extent permitted by law, LB IT Cloud SAS is not
liable for any damage arising from their use.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

None. Every file in this repository was written by LB IT Cloud SAS: the tool
uses no library, and the offline file embeds no third-party code or typeface.
The test runner (vitest) is installed separately, under its own licence, and is
not part of this repository.


